From: AlexProgrammerDE <40795980+AlexProgrammerDE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 22:11:19 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(equipment): synchronize native armor attributes

Bedrock does not send player armor attributes, so the Java armor meter remains empty despite equipped armor. Derive protection and toughness from the authoritative armor container and send standard Java attributes after equipment changes, joins, respawns, and dimension changes. Batch full replacements and suppress duplicate totals.

BDS 1.26.51.1 build 51061372 equippable queries establish vanilla values, including copper armor. Captured ItemRegistry components provide custom wearable protection and declared slots. The target excludes misplaced armor and hand wearables from both totals; preserve those rules and use zero toughness for custom wearables. Snapshot copies do not emit attributes, while restoring the actual armor container recomputes totals.
